nishing-a-development-branch: Use when implementation is complete, all tests pass, and you need to decide how to integrate the work - guides completion of development work by presenting structured options for merge, PR, or cleanup\n- entire-internal:github-pr-review: Use when viewing PR review comments, replying to review threads, creating PRs, or changing draft status via gh CLI\n- entire-internal:test-auditor: Audits unit tests for code changed on the current branch — rates existing tests, flags useless ones for removal, and writes missing tests. Use this skill whenever the user wants to evaluate test quality, audit tests, check test effectiveness, improve test coverage for their branch, find weak or redundant tests, or asks things like \"are my tests good?\", \"do I have enough tests?\", \"audit my tests\", \"clean up my tests\", or \"what tests am I missing?\". Also trigger when the user mentions \"test coverage\", \"test gaps\", \"redundant tests\", \"flaky tests\", \"useless tests\", or \"test quality\" in the context of a feature branch.\n- entire-internal:oss-triage: Triage OSS issues and PRs for entireio/cli. Run with subcommands: issues, prs, all\n- frontend-design:frontend-design: Create distinctive, production-grade frontend interfaces with high design quality. Use this skill when the user asks to build web components, pages, or applications. Generates creative, polished code that avoids generic AI aesthetics.\n- codex:codex-cli-runtime: Internal helper contract for calling the codex-companion runtime from Claude Code\n- codex:gpt-5-4-prompting: Internal guidance for composing Codex and GPT-5.4 prompts for coding, review, diagnosis, and research tasks inside the Codex Claude Code plugin\n- codex:codex-result-handling: Internal guidance for presenting Codex helper output back to the user\n- init: Initialize a new CLAUDE.md file with codebase documentation\n- review: Review a pull request\n- security-review: Complete a security review of the pending change