nt `ChunkFilenameSeparator = \".\"` at package level and add a comment referencing the agent package's chunking behavior. Better: move to a typed validation function.\n\n---\n\n### Finding 6: Inconsistent Commit Message Style\n**Location:** `cmd/entire/cli/migrate.go:562`\n\nThe message `\"Write migrated partial generation\\n\"` has a trailing newline (good style), but differs from others:\n- Line 611: `fmt.Sprintf(\"Archive migrated generation: %s\\n\", ...)`  \n- Line 774: `\"Start generation\\n\"`\n- Line 858: `fmt.Sprintf(\"Reset checkpoint before force migration: %s\\n\", ...)`\n\nThe \"Write migrated partial generation\" message is vague; it doesn't say *which* generation or checkpoint. Other messages include the ref name.\n\n**Suggested Fix:** Change to `fmt.Sprintf(\"Write pending checkpoints to /full/current\\n\")` or include the pending checkpoint count for consistency and clarity.\n\n---\n\n### Finding 7: Early State Initialization, Late Validation\n**Location:** `cmd/entire/cli/migrate.go:697-702` (`buildMigratedFullSessionEntrySet()`)\n\nThe function eagerly populates `rawArtifactPaths` before calling `agent.ChunkTranscript()` (line 704), which can error. If chunking fails, the struct with pre-populated paths is discarded, suggesting unclear intent.\n\n**Suggested Fix:** Populate `rawArtifactPaths` after the chunking succeeds, or move the transcript validation earlier. This makes the error path clearer.\n\n---\n\n### Finding 8: Test Assertion Changes Warrant Expanded Coverage\n**Locations:** `cmd/entire/cli/migrate_test.go:296, 327, 496, 501`\n\nThe test `TestMigrateCheckpointsV2_PacksFullGenerationsOldestFirst` now expects `1` checkpoint in `/full/current` (line 327) instead of `0`, reflecting the new behavior. The new test `TestMigrateCheckpointsV2_UnderThresholdKeepsFullGenerationInCurrent` (line 191) verifies under-threshold behavior separately, but:\n- It only checks checkpoint *count* in current, not checkpoint *identity*\n- The assertion at line 