nstead of wrapping, callers should use `FlattenTree` directly with a map, then iterate. Or: add a `FlattenTreeToSlice()` variant in checkpoint/parse_tree.go if slice-based APIs become common. Currently: **don't create the wrapper—call FlattenTree directly in writePendingToCurrent and convert inline if needed.**\n\n---\n\n### **3. `migratedRawArtifactPaths.matches()` reimplements chunked-artifact matching (migrate.go:659-661)**\n\n**Issue:** Pattern `path == transcriptPath || strings.HasPrefix(path, transcriptPath+\".\") || path == hashPath` matches transcript + chunks + hash.\n\n**Existing Utility:** `agent.ChunkFileName()` and `agent.ChunkSuffix = \".%03d\"` define chunk naming. No existing \"does this path belong to this session's transcript\" predicate.\n\n**Why it's there:** Code needs to identify which entries to delete when re-writing transcripts.\n\n**Fix:** Consider a utility on `migratedRawArtifactPaths` or in agent package:\n```go\n// In agent/chunking.go\nfunc IsTranscriptArtifact(basePath string, fullPath string) bool {\n    return fullPath == basePath || \n           (strings.HasPrefix(fullPath, basePath) && len(fullPath) > len(basePath) && \n            fullPath[len(basePath)] == '.') ||\n           fullPath == basePath + \"_hash.txt\"\n}\n```\nBut this is session-specific (transcript + hash), not agent-generic. **Keep the method but document the chunk suffix assumption.**\n\n---\n\n### **4. Commit message pattern is inconsistent (migrate.go:562 vs paths.go usage)**\n\n**Issue:** `writePendingToCurrent` hardcodes `\"Write migrated partial generation\\n\"` while `writeMigratedFullGeneration` uses `fmt.Sprintf(\"Archive migrated generation: %s\\n\", refName)`.\n\n**Existing Pattern:** Other prune/reset operations use `fmt.Sprintf(\"Reset checkpoint before force migration: %s\\n\", cpID)` (line 720). No centralized commit message factory.\n\n**Fix:** Define constants in migrate.go:\n```go\nconst (\n    migrateCommitMsg = \"Write migrated partial generation\"\n    migrateArchiveMsg = \"Archive migrated generation: %s\"\n    migratePruneMsg = \"Reset checkpoint before force migration: %s\"\n)\n```\nThen use `fmt.Sprintf(migrateCommitMsg + \"\\n\", ...)` to ensure consistency and enable future refactoring.\n\n---\n\n### **5. Test helper pattern is repeated (migrate_test.go: lines 191-197, 325-329, 544-550, etc.)**\n\n**Issue:** Every test that modifies `migrateMaxCheckpointsPerGeneration` repeats:\n```go\noldMax := migrateMaxCheckpointsPerGeneration\nmigrateMaxCheckpointsPerGeneration = N\nt.Cleanup(func() { migrateMaxCheckpointsPerGeneration = oldMax })\n```\n\n**Existing Pattern:** No test helper.\n\n**Fix:** Add a test helper in migrate_test.go:\n```go\nfunc withMaxCheckpointsPerGeneration(t *testing.T, max int) {\n    oldMax := migrateMaxCheckpointsPerGeneration\n    migrateMaxCheckpointsPerGeneration = max\n    t.Cleanup(func() { migrateMaxCheckpointsPerGeneration = oldMax })\n}\n```\nThen: `withMaxCheckpointsPerGeneration(t, 5)` (4 test sites).\n\n---\n\n### **Summary Table**\n\n| Location | New Code | Existing Utility | Improvement |\n|----------|----------|------------------|-------------|\n| migrate.go:505–570 | `writePendingToCurrent` ref logic | `V2GitStore.updateRef()` | Extract to parameterized helper |\n| migrate.go:749–760 | `flattenMigratedFullEntries` | `checkpoint.FlattenTree()` | Remove wrapper; use directly |\n| migrate.go:659–661 | `migratedRawArtifactPaths.matches()` | `agent.ChunkSuffix` | Document assumption; consider utility |\n| migrate.go:548,562 | Commit message strings | None | Define constants for reuse |\n| migrate_test.go (4x) | Temp variable restore | None | Extract test helper |\n\n**Recommended priority:** Fix #1 (updateRef), #5 (test helper), then #4 (constants). #2 and #3 are lower-impact (API consistency vs. scope-specific logic)."}]}]},"uuid":"8c363560-9fca-4001-918c-864549cca808","timestamp":"2026-05-05T22:45:43.654Z","toolUseResult":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are review